dart:ffi Abi.current() returns androidArm64/androidX64/... on Termux, which
falls into the default branch and throws "Unsupported host platform". Map the
Android ABIs to the matching linux host platforms so cache directories
(linux-arm64, linux-x64) are resolved the same way as on desktop Linux.

--- a/packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/base/os.dart	2026-10-30 03:44:14.991864565 +0000
+++ b/packages/flutter_tools/lib/src/base/os.dart	2026-10-30 03:44:18.668359981 +0000
@@ -151,6 +151,9 @@
       Abi.linuxX64 => HostPlatform.linux_x64,
       Abi.linuxArm64 => HostPlatform.linux_arm64,
       Abi.linuxRiscv64 => HostPlatform.linux_riscv64,
+      Abi.androidArm64 => HostPlatform.linux_arm64,
+      Abi.androidX64 => HostPlatform.linux_x64,
+      Abi.androidRiscv64 => HostPlatform.linux_riscv64,
       Abi.windowsX64 => HostPlatform.windows_x64,
       Abi.windowsArm64 => HostPlatform.windows_arm64,
       _ => throw UnsupportedError('Unsupported host platform: $_currentAbi'),
